      "hardware_label": "Radeon AI Pro R9700",
      "notes": "DeepSeek V4 Flash ROCmFP2, HYBRID dual-device: AMD Radeon AI PRO R9700 (gfx1201, 32GB) = hip:0 as primary compute device, PLUS the Ryzen AI Max 395 Strix Halo integrated GPU (Radeon 8060S, gfx1151) = hip:1 sharing 128GB unified system memory, connected over Oculink with GPU peer access enabled. The hardware schema is a discriminated union and cannot express discrete+unified together, so only the R9700 is listed in the gpus array; the iGPU's participation is disclosed here. Weights DeepSeek-V4-Flash-ROCMFP2-STRIX.gguf (102.3 GB, engine-native ROCmFP2 format; no matching LocalMaxxing quant enum, MXFP4 chosen as nearest FP4 label) + DSpark speculative draft DeepSeek-V4-Flash-DSpark-draft-Q4RMFP4-denseF16.gguf (11.3 GB, q=4). Decode-only measurement: median of 3 timed 128-token generations after 2 warmups, temperature 0, ~1956-token prompt, single concurrency, server-authoritative timing: 51.7 / 52.0 / 52.0 tok/s (median 52.0). DSpark acceptance ~0.99, outputs byte-identical across runs. IMPORTANT APPROXIMATION: this run used top-4 experts/token to reproduce a published headline figure; the quality-default 6-experts/token profile measured ~45.5 tok/s on the same rig. Prefill throughput, TTFT, power draw and peak VRAM were not recorded for this run, and the source blog's 415 tok/s prefill was NOT reproduced (decode only). Cold-prefill enforcement was not instrumented.",
